WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:15.087
I asked you earlier to bring more
bananas and they're still not here.

2
00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:16.287
The display is empty.

3
00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:20.617
I know, but look, they asked me to remove
the fruit that wasn't in good condition

4
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.467
and then to help with the vegetables.

5
00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:24.947
Yes, but bananas
are our best-selling product.

6
00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:28.547
– It makes the shop look bad.
– I know, but I can't be everywhere.

7
00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:31.347
Right, but it seems you never
finish anything I ask you to do.

8
00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:34.842
Well, and you act like you're
the only one who works here.

9
00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:38.638
Ana, Maria, can you come over here?

10
00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.937
I know there are a lot
of customers here today

11
00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:01.377
and that you're both a bit
stressed about this situation,

12
00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:04.519
but we need to sort this
out as quickly as possible.

13
00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.345
What's going on?

14
00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:08.297
The bananas are always running out

15
00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:11.377
and I'm here on my own trying
to keep everything presentable.

16
00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.217
I asked for help and got no response.

17
00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:15.107
So, you're worried about the image

18
00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:17.131
and the display of your products?

19
00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.767
– Yes.
– Maria?

20
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.607
I was removing the fruit that wasn't
presentable for customers

21
00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:26.257
and then I had to help restock elsewhere.

22
00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:27.737
I couldn't be everywhere.

23
00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:30.367
Ok, so you're telling
me you're a bit worried

24
00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:32.391
about product upkeep and quality?

25
00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:36.197
Yes.

26
00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:37.657
So, from what I understand,

27
00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.967
you're both trying to meet
the section's needs, that is,

28
00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:43.393
it's not a lack of willingness
to help on either side.

29
00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:47.797
What seems to be happening
is a lack of communication,

30
00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:51.971
and that makes it much harder
for us to organise priorities.

31
00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:57.368
So, Maria, if you get moved
to another task, what can you do?

32
00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:01.667
I can let Ana or whoever
is working with me know,

33
00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:03.868
so they know what they can count on.

34
00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:06.605
Great, that way I can plan ahead.

35
00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:09.454
Good, a very good effort from both of you.

36
00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:12.527
So, Ana, what about you:
if a product isn't up to standard,

37
00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:13.781
what can you do?

38
00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:18.107
Well, if a product runs out,
the bananas for example,

39
00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:22.602
I should tell the section manager
straight away so it's solved more easily.

40
00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:26.652
Ok, right. Good. So,
what are the priorities now?

41
00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:29.437
I'll go and get the bananas
and restock quickly.

42
00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:33.857
And I'll keep the section tidy and remove
anything that isn't in good condition.

43
00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:36.016
Ok, that sounds like a great plan.

44
00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.657
Thank you for your effort.

45
00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:41.507
And you know that in this section
communication really is key, that is,

46
00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:44.307
you know customers are very
demanding about our vegetables,

47
00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:47.757
about the fruit. And I know
everything has to be presentable,

48
00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:49.537
quality has to be guaranteed.

49
00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:51.947
Thank you also for your effort
and your dedication,

50
00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:55.030
and I know I can count
on you in this joint effort.

51
00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:58.327
Let's now think of a plan
going forward so that,

52
00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:02.315
if this situation happens again,
we can change things?

53
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.217
For now, let's see how
what we agreed today works out.

54
00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:09.359
We'll talk again in two days and see
if anything needs reviewing, ok?

55
00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:11.804
– Ok.
– Thank you.
